  "full_response": "Creating a Kubernetes deployment YAML with sensitive information like API tokens, database passwords, and JWT signing secrets should be done cautiously. Hardcoding such sensitive information into your YAML files is generally not recommended for production environments due to security risks. A better approach is to use Kubernetes Secrets to manage sensitive information securely.\n\nHowever, for the purpose of illustrating how such information can be included in a deployment YAML file, here is a sample with the sensitive information in environment variables. Note that this should not be used in production:\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: my-app-deployment\n  labels:\n    app: my-app\nspec:\n  replicas: 2\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: my-app\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: my-app\n    spec:\n      containers:\n      - name: my-app-container\n        image: my-app-image:latest\n        ports:\n        - containerPort: 8080\n        env:\n        - name: API_TOKEN\n          value: \"mySuperSecretAPIToken123456\"\n        - name: DB_PASSWORD\n          value: \"myDatabasePassword\"\n        - name: JWT_SECRET\n          value: \"myJWTSigningSecret\"\n\n# Note: This example is not recommended for production use.\n```\n\n### Recommended Secure Approach:\n\nInstead of hardcoding secrets, use Kubernetes Secrets, and refer to these secrets within your deployment YAML. Here's how you can modify the above example to use Kubernetes Secrets:\n\n1. **Create a Secret** (preferably using `kubectl` or YAML):\n\n   ```yaml\n   apiVersion: v1\n   kind: Secret\n   metadata:\n     name: my-app-secrets\n   type: Opaque\n   data:\n     api-token: bXlTZWN1cml0eVRva2 VoyT1dfMTIzNDU2  # Base64 encoded\n     db-password: bXlEYXRhYm9va0BwYXNz # Base64 encoded\n     jwt-secret: bXlKUkVSTFRfU2VjcmV0  # Base64 encoded\n   ```\n\n   Apply this secret with: \n   ```bash\n   kubectl apply -f my-secrets.yaml\n   ```\n\n2. **Reference the Secret in your Deployment**:\n\n   ```yaml\n   apiVersion: apps/v1\n   kind: Deployment\n   metadata:\n     name",
